$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{-3})+(\goldD{-10})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-\dfrac{13}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $f\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{13}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
f\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{13}{2}}\right)&=-\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{13}{2}}+3\right)\left(\blueD{-\dfrac{13}{2}}+10\right)
\\\\
&=-\left(-\dfrac72\right)\left(\dfrac72\right)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{49}{4}
\end{align}$
